# Development workflow

Understand the task before editing. Identify the allowed scope. Production application work happens only inside an approved increment task (today, INC-001 through `fabrica/tareas/`). Do not create `apps/api`, `apps/web`, a schema, or a migration unless the task explicitly approves that work.

- Do not modify unrelated files.
- Do not install a dependency without justification that the task approved.
- Do not refactor opportunistically. Preserve existing behavior unless the change is intentional.
- Prefer a small reviewable change. Do not combine unrelated logical changes in one task.
- Run the validation that the touched files require. For the domain map, that is `npm run lint:map` and `npm run build:map` when those files change.
- Report the checks that were actually run. Never claim that tests passed if they were not run.
- Do not commit when the task is review-only. Do not push, open a Pull Request, or merge unless the user explicitly asks.
- Leave an out-of-scope opportunity as a finding. Do not implement it in the same change.

A review does not edit files unless the user explicitly asks for the edit.

For branches, commits meant for `main`, Pull Requests, CI, review, and merge, follow [docs/development/github-workflow.md](../../docs/development/github-workflow.md). This rule does not copy that guide. It does not set framework coding standards or a coverage percentage.
